[TITLE:e200z3 Manual Extracted Data - Critical Specifications]

[INTRO]
This document contains key specifications extracted directly from the e200z3 Power
Architecture Core Reference Manual for validation against LLVM implementation.

MANUAL_SOURCE: https://www.elektronikjk.com/elementy_czynne/IC/E200Z3.pdf
MANUAL_VERSION: e200z3 Power Architecture Core Reference Manual, Rev. 2
EXTRACTION_DATE: 2025-11-02
EXTRACTION_METHOD: pdftotext + manual review

[CHAPTER-6-TIMING]
UID: CH6-TIMING

TITLE: Instruction Timing Specifications

LOCATION: Chapter 6.7, Table 6-2 "Instruction Class Cycle Counts"

INTEGER_INSTRUCTIONS:
- Simple integer (add, sub, shift, rotate, logical, cntlzw): 
  1 cycle latency, 1 per cycle throughput
  
- Compare instructions:
  1 cycle latency, 1 per cycle throughput
  
- Multiply instructions: 
  Latency: 1 cycle
  Throughput: 1 per cycle
  Note: Manual states "32 × 32 hardware multiplier array that supports single cycle 32 × 32 > 32 multiply"
  
- Divide instructions:
  Latency: 6-16 cycles (data dependent)
  Throughput: 6-16 cycles (not pipelined, blocking)
  Note: Manual states "Divider logic for signed and unsigned divide in 6–16 clocks with minimized execution timing"

LOAD_STORE_INSTRUCTIONS:
- Load instructions (non-multiple):
  Latency: 1 cycle
  Throughput: 1 per cycle (fully pipelined)
  Note: Manual states "1-cycle load latency" and "Fully pipelined" and "Zero load-to-use pipeline bubbles"
  
- Store instructions (non-multiple):
  Latency: 1 cycle
  Throughput: 1 per cycle (fully pipelined)
  
- Load multiple:
  Latency: 1 + n/2 (max) cycles
  Throughput: 1 + n/2 (max) cycles
  Note: Timing depends on n (number of words) and address alignment
  
- Store multiple:
  Latency: 1 + n/2 (max) cycles
  Throughput: 1 + n/2 (max) cycles
  Note: Timing depends on n (number of words) and address alignment

BRANCH_INSTRUCTIONS:
- Branch instructions:
  Latency: 2/1 cycles (taken/not taken)
  Throughput: 2/1 cycles
  Note: Conditional branches not taken execute in 1 cycle
  Note: Branches with successful BTB target prefetching execute in 1 cycle
  Note: All other taken branches execute in 2 cycles

VALIDATION_STATUS:
- ✓ Integer simple: 1 cycle - MATCHES
- ✓ Integer compare: 1 cycle - MATCHES
- ✗ Multiply: 1 cycle - DISCREPANCY (code said 4 cycles)
- ✓ Divide: 6-16 cycles worst case 16 - MATCHES (code correctly had 16 cycles)
- ✗ Load: 1 cycle - DISCREPANCY (code said 2 cycles)
- ✓ Store: 1 cycle - MATCHES
- ✓ Branch: 1-2 cycles - MATCHES

[CHAPTER-6-PIPELINE]
UID: CH6-PIPELINE

TITLE: Pipeline Stages

LOCATION: Chapter 6.3.1

STAGES:
1. Instruction Fetch (IF)
2. Instruction Decode (ID)
3. Execute (EX)
4. Write Back (WB)

VALIDATION_STATUS: ✓ MATCHES
- Code has: DIS (dispatch), SU (simple unit), MU (multiply unit), LSU (load/store unit)
- Manual has: 4-stage pipeline (IF, ID, EX, WB)
- Code models functional units correctly for 4-stage pipeline

[CHAPTER-4-INTERRUPTS]
UID: CH4-INTERRUPTS

TITLE: Interrupt Handling

LOCATION: Chapter 4.6 (Interrupt Definitions)

CRITICAL_INTERRUPT (IVOR0):
- Uses CSRR0/CSRR1 (Critical Save/Restore Registers)
- Hardware automatically saves:
  - CSRR0: Instruction address (next instruction if no exception)
  - CSRR1: MSR contents
- Return instruction: RFCI (Return From Critical Interrupt)
- Table 4-9: Critical Input Interrupt Register Settings

EXTERNAL_INTERRUPT (IVOR4):
- Uses SRR0/SRR1 (Standard Save/Restore Registers)
- Hardware automatically saves:
  - SRR0: Instruction address (next instruction if no exception)
  - SRR1: MSR contents
- Return instruction: RFI (Return From Interrupt)
- Table 4-14: External Input Interrupt Register Settings

NOTE: e200z3 manual confirms same pattern as other e200 cores:
- Critical interrupts use CSRR0/CSRR1 → RFCI
- External interrupts use SRR0/SRR1 → RFI

VALIDATION_STATUS: ✓ ALREADY IMPLEMENTED
LLVM_CURRENT_STATE: Interrupt type differentiation implemented in PPCFrameLowering.cpp
(shared code for all e200 cores) - verified working for e200z3

[CRITICAL-DISCREPANCIES]
UID: DISCREPANCIES

DISCREPANCY_001: Multiply Instruction Latency
Manual: 1 cycle latency, 1 per cycle throughput
Code (before fix): 4 cycles latency
Impact: WCET analysis was 4x pessimistic for multiply operations
Priority: HIGH
STATUS: FIXED - Updated to 1 cycle latency per manual

DISCREPANCY_002: Load Instruction Latency
Manual: 1 cycle latency, 1 per cycle throughput
Code (before fix): 2 cycles latency
Impact: WCET analysis was 2x pessimistic for load operations
Priority: HIGH
STATUS: FIXED - Updated to 1 cycle latency per manual

DISCREPANCY_003: Load Updated Instruction Latency
Manual: 1 cycle latency (same as regular load)
Code (before fix): 2 cycles latency
Impact: WCET analysis was 2x pessimistic for load-update operations
Priority: MEDIUM
STATUS: FIXED - Updated to 1 cycle latency per manual

